    <statement><p>Find the domain of the vector functions, <m>\mathbf r(t)</m>, listed below.</p>
<p>using .</p>
<p>a) 
<m>\mathbf r(t) = \left \langle \ln(10 t), \sqrt{t  + 9}, \displaystyle\frac{1}{\sqrt{15 - t}} \right \rangle</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>b)
<m>\mathbf r(t) = \left \langle \sqrt{t  - 6 }, \sin(4 t), t^2 \right \rangle</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>c)
<m>\mathbf r(t) = \left \langle \ e^{-6 t}, \displaystyle\frac{t}{\sqrt{t^2 - 16}}, t^{1/3} \right \rangle</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(0,15\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left[6,\infty \right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-\infty ,-4\right)\cup \left(4,\infty \right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
